            <ArticleTitle>Transluminal dilatation in the management of mesenteric angina: a report of two cases.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>46-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Two patients with typical clinical and angiographic findings of mesenteric angina are reported. Both remain asymptomatic seven and 11 months respectively, after transluminal dilatation of superior mesenteric artery stenoses.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
